{"understanding":"The supplied code shows that file snapshots are written through a temporary directory, flushed and optionally synced, finalized with CRC metadata, atomically renamed, then older snapshots are reaped. Snapshot installation persists and validates the received snapshot before restoring the FSM, updating applied and snapshot indexes, restoring configuration, and compacting logs. However, the orchestration that captures the FSM index, establishes the snapshot boundary, performs compaction, and reconstructs application state is not supplied. The existing G1/O1 applicability therefore remains unresolved.","requests":[{"file":"fsm.go","start_line":16,"end_line":285,"reason":"Inspect FSM snapshot capture, restore, applied-index ownership, and completion/error behavior."},{"file":"snapshot.go","start_line":15,"end_line":278,"reason":"Inspect snapshot interfaces and contracts for capture, persistence, restore, and index semantics."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":965,"end_line":1205,"reason":"Inspect snapshot scheduling, FSM index establishment, compaction, and ordering relative to application."},{"file":"log.go","start_line":1,"end_line":192,"reason":"Inspect log-store deletion and compaction semantics needed to determine whether snapshot persistence is the only recoverable representation."},{"file":"inmem_snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":113,"reason":"Inspect the concrete in-memory snapshot behavior and whether it provides applicable restore/index guarantees."}],"responsibilities":[],"patch":{"claims":[],"bindings":[],"relations":[],"units":[],"expected_versions":[],"rationale":"No graph changes are justified until the missing capture, restore, and compaction behavior is read.","gaps":["The supplied snapshot-store implementation does not establish which FSM state/index was captured.","The supplied install path does not establish whether restored FSM state is equivalent to replay through the compacted index.","Compaction and deletion error handling outside installSnapshot remain unread.","The applicability and guarantees of the concrete FSM and snapshot implementations remain unresolved."]},"exploration_requests":[{"reason":"Resolve the snapshot capture-to-compaction boundary before deriving or checking G1/O1.","responsibility_ids":["RESP1","RESP2","RESP3"],"requests":[{"file":"fsm.go","start_line":16,"end_line":285,"reason":"Trace FSM Snapshot and Restore calls, applied-index state, and asynchronous completion."},{"file":"snapshot.go","start_line":15,"end_line":278,"reason":"Read SnapshotStore, SnapshotSink, FSMSnapshot, and restore contracts."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":965,"end_line":1205,"reason":"Trace takeSnapshot, snapshot index selection, persistence completion, and compactLogs ordering."},{"file":"log.go","start_line":1,"end_line":192,"reason":"Trace DeleteRange, StoreLogs, and log-store boundary behavior."},{"file":"inmem_snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":113,"reason":"Check whether the concrete in-memory snapshot backend supplies relevant capture and restore behavior."}]}],"limitations":["No new audit unit is proposed because the required capture and compaction producer behavior is unread.","The current material supports review of file snapshot durability and install sequencing, but not the full recoverability obligation.","No concrete suspicion or confirmed violation can be stated without the missing FSM, snapshot orchestration, and log-store ranges."]}
